title: Ch2
position: 404,-519
---
<<if get_flag("Blind")>>
	The work was hard, but it came with its rewards. 
	<<if get_flag("dadMech")>>
	Your help was essential in keeping the whole station running.
	<<endif>>
	These people really believed in what they were doing and so did you.
	And they might even have had a shot at creating a free Jovian system. 
	But unfortunately with the come of the successful treaty that stopped the Shatter, the Blinds lose a lot of their followers. 
	That on top of the opening of the Pons and the arrival of both Venuvian and Martian military force, drove the rebellion on the ground.
<<elseif get_flag("Martian")>>
	Apart from some minor incidents here and there the conflict never exploded into a real war. 
	<<if get_flag ("dadSoldier")>>
	Your job was mostly containing small uprising here and there in the system, but not much more. 
	<<elseif get_flag("dadMech")>>
	Your job ended up being fixing and refurbishing old spy drones from earth into full fledged support systems for the inhabitants of the jovian system.
	<<endif>>
	But luckly those days ended when the Marsuvian alliance managed to secure a successful treaty with earth. 
	The latter would open back up the water supplies to the jovian, and give them partial freedom while remaining in control of europa and io's resources.
	While martian and Venuvian would delopy troops in the system so to avoid father endangerment in the jovian. 	
<<endif>>
Everything that happened those days it's now a fudge. From back then you remember the relief. 
Not having to worry about water anymore. 
You remember the sorrow.
For those you lost. 
The anger.
Of knowing all that could have been avoided

But you also remember her.
How safe she made you feel. 
You remember that old sofa, where you grew closer. 
where you hopped you'd have grown old together.

But here it is again, the memories are getting fuzzy.
Everything spinning. 

->What is happening
->Try to relax

The hospital was cold. 
You always liked hospitals, how sterile they're. 
In how they're designed to be as efficient and secure as possible.
there's something calming such an environment.
But nothing is calming right now. 
The overused plastic chair is too Squeaky and stigg to be sitting in. 
The lights too flickery. 
When the doctor asked you to leave, and the nurse escorted you out, you knew something was wrong. 
You compiled, but now you regret it.

The next thing you know the doctor is in front of you
-> Aks how's your Wife doing.
	<<if adjust_status(0,1,0,0)>><<endif>>
-> Ask how's your child doing.
	<<if adjust_status(0,0,1,0)>><<endif>>
<<jump Ch3>>
